{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CghToEYQ6sLJN4kzDyAMs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your message came through with no sequence attached — just the question. Nothing to BLAST yet.\n\nI confirmed the tools I'd use are live and ready, so once you paste it this is a single step:\n\n- **`blast_sequence`** (NCBI BLAST, `program: blastp`, `database: nr`) — primary identification, returns best-hit title, E-value, % identity, % coverage\n- **`query_uniprot`** — to pull the function/domain annotation for whatever the top hit turns out to be\n- **`query_alphafold`** — if you also want the predicted structure and per-residue pLDDT for comparison against the structure file you extracted it from\n\nPaste the sequence as raw amino acids or FASTA; either works. A couple of things that would help but aren't required:\n\n1. **The structure file itself**, or its header — if it's a PDB/mmCIF download, the `HEADER`/`COMPND`/`SEQRES` records or `_struct.title` often name the protein outright, which is faster and more definitive than a BLAST round-trip. If it's an AlphaFold model, the filename usually embeds the UniProt accession (e.g. `AF-P01308-F1`), which answers the question directly.\n2. **Which chain** you pulled, if the structure is a multi-chain complex — otherwise you may have concatenated two different proteins into one sequence, which will make the BLAST result look chimeric and confusing.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging in advance: sequences read out of coordinate files are often *not* the full biological sequence. Disordered loops and unresolved termini are frequently missing from crystal structures, and expression tags (His6, TEV sites, GST/MBP fusions) are sometimes present. That won't usually stop identification — BLAST handles partial queries fine — but it does mean the coverage figure may come back low even for a correct, confident hit, and residue numbering from the structure may not match UniProt numbering.\n\n## ANSWER\n\nUNABLE: No sequence was included in your message — the paste appears to have been dropped. Send the amino acid sequence (raw or FASTA) and I'll run blastp against `nr` and report the top hit with its E-value, identity, and coverage."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10199,"cache_read_input_tokens":19967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10199},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a34d36d-c9c9-4349-be83-877b08187acd","uuid":"10b12553-61a3-4888-b203-5fd4a3aa5ab9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:05:16.268Z","request_id":"req_011CghToEF3KXujwZADZKT4s"}
